      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Severity: NC State rates the poison medium (the 01e baseline was 1); the ASPCA lists dogs and cats as toxic with oral pain, swelling, drooling and vomiting. Graded 2, the agent's mapping. RHS (cultivar 'Pink Allusion') says harmful if swallowed and an irritant to skin and eyes. Size is NC State (3 to 6 ft by 1 to 2 ft, upper values); RHS 1.5 to 2.5 m by up to 0.5 m. Humidity: NC State high, RHS medium; temperature: warm on both, no range. Growth rate: not stated. Young plants are shrubby and turn vining with age, so habit changes over time."
      },
